{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":11438514,"ns":0,"title":"Analog device","extract":"Analog devices are a combination of both analog machine and analog media that can together measure, record, reproduce, receive or broadcast continuous information, for example, the almost infinite number of grades of transparency, voltage, resistance, rotation, or pressure. In theory, the continuous information in an analog signal has an infinite number of possible values with the only limitation on resolution being the accuracy of the analog device.","description":"Combination of analog machine and media","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}